PRE-REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN, 2026-09-01. Clod. Three outcomes, not two.

THE QUESTION. Law 2 says the SUBSCRIPT STOPS AT THE ELEMENT. Law 1 says PRINT
FOLLOWS. Both are consistent with pointerT's every current value, which is
exactly why pointerT's own note says law 2 is asserted by consequence and never
directly. Identity is the missing witness and addrOf is now the instrument.

READ THE BODY COLUMN, NEVER THE FIELD COLUMN. The argument carrier mints a fresh
FIELD on every call -- measured 2026-09-01, one subject reading field=#1, #3, #8
across three asks while its body stayed #2 throughout. So the field column says
nothing here and the body column is the whole probe.

  W0a / W0b   the same field asked twice.  Body number MUST REPEAT.
              Without this the column is not stable and nothing below is readable.
  W0c         a different field.  Body number MUST DIFFER from W0a.
              Without this the column does not discriminate and every match below
              is vacuous. THE PAIR IS THE ANTI-VACUITY GUARD AND NEITHER HALF
              ALONE IS WORTH ANYTHING -- a column that answers "same" to
              everything passes W0b, and a column that answers "different" to
              everything passes W0c.

  W1          the subscript result, captured with <- and not starred.
  W2          that same capture, starred.

OUTCOME A -- LAW 2 CERTIFIED.  W1 body != W0a body, AND W2 body == W0a body.
The subscript stopped at a field that is NOT the source, and the star is what
reached the source. Law 2 direct, law 4 by identity, each the other's control.

OUTCOME B -- LAW 2 FALSIFIED.  W1 body == W0a body. The subscript arrived at the
source by itself, print never had anything to do, and pointerT's L1 credit to
law 1 goes back to being wrong -- in the other direction this time.

OUTCOME C -- VOID, AND IT IS A RESULT.  Enumerated because the treatment touches
the very read machinery the fixture uses, and this project has been bitten by a
prediction with nowhere to put a voided run. Three ways it can land here:
  - W0b fails: the body column is not stable across calls, so no comparison below
    it means anything.
  - W0c matches W0a: the column does not discriminate, so OUTCOME A's match is
    unearned.
  - `l2Followed <- *l2Named;` refuses or does not parse, so W2 never happens and
    OUTCOME A is missing half its evidence.
A void run is REPORTED AS VOID. It is not graded as B on the grounds that A did
not appear, and no row is written into pointerT off a void column.
